; std/loops: a macro calling itself through a lazy gate. One step per round,
; and the value the stop rule judged is the value returned.
; expect: calls >=3
; expect: clean
; expect: answers
((# std/loops)
 (~ tighten (v) (-> v "Shorten this by one word. Return only the result."))
 (~ short-enough (v) (-> v "Is this three words or fewer? Answer exactly 1 or 0."))
 (std-loop "A rather long and quite verbose sentence" tighten short-enough))
